Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:50:04 +0000
Subject: glider matrix

Give the glider's matrix inverse a whole 4x4 local.

The glider's update (func_L08_003CDF98, functional C shared by Tabora,
Dobbo and Grelbin) inverts its moby's matrix in state 0 with
func_00283698, which writes all 64 bytes of a 4x4 matrix. The functional
C passed the 16-byte local v30, so the inverse ran 48 bytes past it, the
last 16 beyond the function's frame. Retail passes a 64-byte stack area.
The matrix now goes into a local of its own.
---
 nonmatching/functional/func_L08_003CDF98.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nonmatching/functional/func_L08_003CDF98.c b/nonmatching/functional/func_L08_003CDF98.c
index a7bc4db..5950419 100644
--- a/nonmatching/functional/func_L08_003CDF98.c
+++ b/nonmatching/functional/func_L08_003CDF98.c
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-/* functional: medium. From the near-miss draft; its level data was named D_XXXXXXXX (boot) for addresses at or above 0x1A7C80 and is now D_L08_ (lesson 12). Gated SAME on 4 calls, which ran only 181 of 1684 retail instructions; every unrun block was then read against retail (2026-11-02) and six slips fixed: state 6's exit to state 1 has no func_002A7470 call; the func_002ABBB8 stack arguments are 1, -1, 0 (not 1, 0, -1); state 10's limit is min(dist, d+0x94), not the B0138 tuning value; the state >= 7 particle size is 0.07, not 0.0425; the particle field at +8 is a byte; the 0x70 and 0xA0 id lists are words; two constants now carry retail's exact bits (0.060000002f = 0x3D75C290, 1.01f = 0x3F8147AE). Locals and the shared tails differ from retail's layout only. */
+/* functional: medium. From the near-miss draft; its level data was named D_XXXXXXXX (boot) for addresses at or above 0x1A7C80 and is now D_L08_ (lesson 12). Gated SAME on 4 calls, which ran only 181 of 1684 retail instructions; every unrun block was then read against retail (2026-11-02) and six slips fixed: state 6's exit to state 1 has no func_002A7470 call; the func_002ABBB8 stack arguments are 1, -1, 0 (not 1, 0, -1); state 10's limit is min(dist, d+0x94), not the B0138 tuning value; the state >= 7 particle size is 0.07, not 0.0425; the particle field at +8 is a byte; the 0x70 and 0xA0 id lists are words; two constants now carry retail's exact bits (0.060000002f = 0x3D75C290, 1.01f = 0x3F8147AE). Locals and the shared tails differ from retail's layout only. State 0's inverse (func_00283698, a whole 4x4 matrix) goes into a 64-byte local, as retail's 64-byte stack area: into the 16-byte v30 it wrote 48 bytes past it, the last 16 beyond the frame. */
 /* Hero-NPC state machine shared by Tabora, Dobbo and Grelbin. Retained
  * reconstruction, not functional-gated. USA v1.01: 6,632/6,736 bytes, 0/3 places
  * (2026-11-01); the earlier source emitted 6,624 bytes.
@@ -143,6 +143,7 @@ extern int func_L08_003CDB78(void *, void *);
 void func_L08_003CDF98(u8 *obj)
 {
     Vec saved, v30, v40, v50;
+    Vec inverse[4]; /* func_00283698 writes a whole 4x4 matrix */
     u8 *d, *p, *a70, *a98, *aA0, *aB0;
     int i, n, id;
     float f, t;
@@ -165,8 +166,8 @@ void func_L08_003CDF98(u8 *obj)
         DF(8) = DF(8) + D_L08_001AFFD0;
         func_0029FCC0(obj, 8, d + 0x30);
         func_00282CF0(d + 0x30, obj + 0x10, d + 0x30);
-        func_00283698(&v30, obj + 0xC0);
-        func_002830C0(d + 0x30, d + 0x30, &v30);
+        func_00283698(inverse, obj + 0xC0);
+        func_002830C0(d + 0x30, d + 0x30, inverse);
         DF(0x3C) = 1.0f;
         if (OB(0x43) != 0)
             func_002A7470(obj, 0, 0, 0xA);
